    <tit|Q Learning>

    \;

    The Q-Learning algorithm goes as follows:

    <\itemize-dot>
      <item>1. Set the <math|\<gamma\>> parameter, and environment rewards in
      matrix <math|R>.

      <item>2. Initialize matrix <math|Q> to zero.

      <item>3. For each episode:

      <\itemize-minus>
        <item> Select a random initial state.

        <item> Do While the goal state hasn't been reached.

        <\itemize-arrow>
          \ Select one among all possible actions for the current state.

          \ Using this possible action, consider going to the next state.

          \ Get maximum Q value for this next state based on all possible
          actions.

          \ Compute:\ 

          <with|math-display|true|<space|4em><math|Q<around*|(|s,a|)>=R<around*|(|s,a|)>+\<gamma\>max<rsub|<wide|a|~>>Q<around*|(|<wide|s|~>,<wide|a|~>|)>>>

          \ Set the next state as the current state.
        </itemize-arrow>
      </itemize-minus>
    </itemize-dot>

    \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 

    \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 

    \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <tit|Q>

    \;

